OPAL

Performance-first Linux + Apple Silicon macOS remote desktop.

Linux install

Fedora 44+ / Fedora Asahi
  sudo dnf install -y https://mirrors.rpmfusion.org/free/fedora/rpmfusion-free-release-$(rpm -E %fedora).noarch.rpm
  sudo dnf install -y --allowerasing gcc-c++ make pkgconf-pkg-config SDL3-devel openssl-devel ffmpeg ffmpeg-devel pipewire pipewire-devel pipewire-pulseaudio libportal libportal-devel xdg-desktop-portal xdg-desktop-portal-kde wl-clipboard curl

CachyOS / Arch Linux
  sudo pacman -S --needed base-devel pkgconf sdl3 openssl ffmpeg pipewire pipewire-pulse libportal xdg-desktop-portal xdg-desktop-portal-kde wl-clipboard curl

Debian 13+ / Ubuntu with SDL3
  sudo apt-get update
  sudo apt-get install -y build-essential pkg-config libsdl3-dev libssl-dev ffmpeg libavformat-dev libavcodec-dev libavutil-dev libswresample-dev libswscale-dev libpipewire-0.3-dev libportal-dev pipewire pipewire-pulse xdg-desktop-portal xdg-desktop-portal-kde wl-clipboard curl

Linux build
  make -j"$(nproc)"
  sudo make install

macOS install

Apple Silicon, macOS 13+:
  brew install pkg-config sdl3 openssl@3 ffmpeg

macOS build
  make -j"$(sysctl -n hw.ncpu)"
  sudo make macos-install

macOS host setup
  run opal and choose "Host this computer"
  OPAL requests Screen Recording for the host and Accessibility for the exact opal-input helper
  if macOS asks for permission, grant it and run opal again to finish setup
  host service: ~/Library/LaunchAgents/de.xt9y.opal.host.plist
  restart host service: opal restart

macOS host permissions
  System Settings -> Privacy & Security -> Screen & System Audio Recording -> allow OPAL/host process
  System Settings -> Privacy & Security -> Accessibility -> allow opal-input
  opal doctor checks both independently

run
  setup / select host --> opal
  connect             --> opal <connection-code>
  debug               --> OPAL_DEBUG=1 opal <connection-code>
  doctor              --> opal doctor

Linux host
  capture   --> PipeWire + libportal + xdg-desktop-portal
  encode    --> persistent in-process FFmpeg/hardware H.264 path
  input     --> /dev/uinput
  clipboard --> wl-clipboard on Wayland, SDL fallback elsewhere
  audio     --> PipeWire/PulseAudio-compatible source
  UDP       --> sendmmsg/recvmmsg batching

macOS host
  capture   --> ScreenCaptureKit, latest-frame CVPixelBuffer path with WindowServer display timestamps
  encode    --> persistent hardware VideoToolbox H.264 low-latency rate control, zero frame delay, on-demand IDR
  input     --> CGEvent through Accessibility-authorized opal-input
  clipboard --> NSPasteboard
  audio     --> ScreenCaptureKit system audio + persistent in-process AAC using the stream synchronization clock
  service   --> per-user launchd LaunchAgent
  UDP       --> nonblocking bounded datagram loop

client
  window/events/input/audio output --> SDL3
  H.264 decode                     --> libavcodec
  presentation                    --> SDL3
  macOS clipboard                 --> NSPasteboard

network
  signed rendezvous + direct end-to-end encrypted UDP + blind encrypted relay fallback
  Tailscale is used when available for the direct tailnet path; local address discovery uses tailscale ip -4
  Linux keeps native UDP batching; macOS uses the same batch contract without packet-copy emulation

verify
  Linux  --> make test && make test-hpi
  macOS  --> make macos-test && opal doctor

  host   --> OPAL_DEBUG=1 opal
  client --> OPAL_DEBUG=1 opal <connection-code>

Windows
  not implemented yet; platform/core interfaces are kept Windows-compatible for a later backend

server
  make deploy-rendezvous
